[WORK]
UID: WORK-SEMANTICS-NIX-EMITTER-PATH
TITLE: The path from the hand-written model document to the Nix behaviour surface
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The logged path from model.json to Nix, so it exists as sdoc before anyone
builds it. SLICE-BEHAVIOUR-MODEL's typed option tree emits the same document
model.json holds today, and a check regenerates and diffs the two, the way
strictdoc-grammar-model-equal does for the grammar. When the emitter lands the
hand-written file is deleted and the emitted one is committed in its place.

Two gotchas measured in the assessment that the surface must respect: Nix
alphabetises attribute keys on emission, so everything ordered in the document
is a list, and the option tree keys entities by name only where order carries
no meaning; and a transition from or to typed as a string passes evaluation
with a typo, so the surface resolves state names against the lifecycle in an
apply pass (addCheck never runs on a submodule, this repository's recorded
invariant).

The Nix side types the model, cross-checks it against the checked grammar
value and emits; it does not evaluate gates, so there is one interpreter. A
full evaluation measured 29 ms with a pinned lib and 825 ms through the flake
registry, so the board reads the committed document and never runs a nix eval
per page.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Operator, 2026-09-03, verbatim: "make sure path to nix if it surfaces is
